{"title":"Fast Way to Calculate Squares (Mental Math)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Have you ever had a time where you see something like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f669669e3e9848f2b03c6b15cb55fc2a258fcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> on AMC 10 or MathLeague.org competitions? But you only have like 30 seconds left and calculating will take too long. So, what will you do? There is this trick I have designed to help with this which is extremely simple. You just take the square before which you know (eg. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a22c275ed0847d82ca1fb6ef7566718533d78cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> in our situation) and add that number to itself not squared then added the number you want to find squared. So, in our case, you get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/849ac6d6d7bcb73dcbc681ca93c6aaa45c400c76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30^2+30+31 = 900+30+31 = 961\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"17\" />This is going to be the answer of the next square of a number. Now, this works because of a formula everyone should know:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5058290bcbaa48a8a7c3ce496adeb9cd014cf4ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2-b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />\nLet's say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is just our previous number squared and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the number right after that. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d481330f3473f921a22037e25f562ecf303a1daf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> and that makes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290f0d6f943c6b30a00986e545c3a2270b24ac56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2-(a+1)^2 = (a-(a+1))(a+(a+1)) \\implies a^2-(a+1)^2 = (-1)(a+(a+1)) \\implies a^2 - (a+1)^2 = -a-(a+1)\\]\" width=\"803\" height=\"20\" />\nNow we can change the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> back into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143a7816ab1c77bff85af5c2f33770f25967332b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2-b^2 = -a-b \\implies \\boxed{b^2 = a^2+a+b}\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"28\" />We can see from this equation that the left side is our number we want to square (like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f669669e3e9848f2b03c6b15cb55fc2a258fcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />) and the right side is the fast way to do it (like the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c5b14b91b61f247da6f0fdac718083911454295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^2+30+31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />). Try using this next time in competitions instead of thoroughly calculating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c59aeaceed43ca41cd398a77ba602895ab448f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />, as an example!\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018084444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 43/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2539/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36878:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018084444 and revision id 285404. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}